/* Generated by scripts/build_legal.py; edit generator/config. */
window.CivicLegalContent = {"version": "2026-11-21", "developerName": "Abdullah Mohiuddin", "supportEmail": "", "privacyUrl": "", "pending": true, "pages": {"privacy": {"title": "Privacy policy", "html": "<p>CivicPost helps you prepare messages to Canadian public offices. You do not create a CivicPost account. This public website requires no sign-in. The Android app is a separate bundled edition.</p>\n<h3>Website agreement</h3><p>If you agree to the terms, CivicPost stores the version you accepted in this browser. You will be asked again when the notice or policies change or when you clear saved app data. If browser storage is unavailable, your choice lasts for this visit.</p><h3>Your drafts and location</h3><p>Names, concerns, recipients and draft text are processed on your device using local templates, not an AI service. Unsaved text stays in the current app session. Saving a draft stores up to ten drafts in this browser or app profile until you delete them. Remember location is optional and stores your chosen location until removed. A saved postal lookup stores one code and public representative data for up to 30 days; it is discarded when next read after expiry. App storage is not separately encrypted by CivicPost. Someone with access to your device or browser profile may be able to read it. The Android app disables Android backup.</p>\n<h3>When information leaves your device</h3><ul><li>The website downloads geographic files from its static host. Contact searches use a separate Cloudflare service, which receives your IP address and the lookup fields you choose, including community, districts, school board, issue category and office search terms. Your name and letter text are not sent to that service. Lookup frequency is limited; contact responses are kept only in this tab’s memory, not the offline cache. The application does not write request logs, although hosting providers process requests under their own policies. Explicitly saved drafts and exported files can contain chosen contacts and remain separate. Offline contact searches are unavailable; previously saved geographic files and drafting can still work. Postal lookup then checks Open North Represent for updates. That request sends the postal code and exposes your network IP address and standard request metadata. Your name and letter are not sent. You can choose a location manually to avoid this request.</li><li>Suggest my city sends a request to BigDataCloud, which uses your IP address to estimate your city. GPS, your name and letter are not sent. Manual location entry avoids that request.</li><li>Opening a mail draft hands the recipients, subject and message to your selected email app or Gmail/Outlook website. Those services then handle the information under their own policies. Pressing Send is a separate action in that service. Offices receiving an email may retain it or disclose it under applicable access-to-information laws.</li><li>QR codes, share links and exported draft files contain the message, recipient addresses and included location details. Anyone who obtains them can read or forward them. Link payloads are in the URL fragment; this is not encryption. Files, screenshots, clipboard copies and emails remain outside CivicPost after export.</li><li>Official source and service links open external sites. They receive ordinary web request information. The hosted website provider may process network/device and sign-in data under its own policy. The Android app bundles its pages and does not require visiting that host.</li></ul>\n<h3>Website visit analytics</h3><p>This public website uses Cloudflare Web Analytics to measure visits, page paths, referring sites, browser/device information, approximate country and loading performance. It does not use analytics cookies or identify returning individuals. Cloudflare receives network request information, including your IP address; its documentation states the IP is discarded at its edge and is not stored in its core analytics databases or logs. CivicPost sends no custom analytics events, letter text, names, selected recipients or form values. Query strings and shared-draft fragments are excluded from the tested beacon payload. Analytics availability depends on your browser and blockers; visits are not a count of unique people or emails sent. The separate Android app does not include this beacon. See <a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/speed/observatory/rum-beacon/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cloudflare analytics data and privacy</a>.</p><h3>Advertising and consent</h3><p>The offline Android edition has no advertising or analytics SDK. This public website has no advertising SDK and uses Cloudflare Web Analytics, described below. An optional Android AdMob edition offers ads only in its separate About &amp; guide screen, after an adult user chooses to enable them. All drafting features work without ads. Google UMP manages available consent and privacy choices before Google Mobile Ads is initialized. Even non-personalized ads may involve device identifiers, IP-derived approximate location, app interactions, diagnostics and fraud-prevention data. CivicPost does not pass your letter, selected offices, issue, name or postal code to the ad SDK. The ad SDK is not connected to the WebView content. Google may process data in other countries under its policies. An ad is not an endorsement by CivicPost or a public office.</p>\n<p>In the AdMob edition, open Advertising choices to manage available Google privacy options or turn ads off. Turning off ads prevents future app-initiated ad requests; it does not erase data already handled by Google. The test installer has no ad SDK. Declining optional ads never blocks the app.</p>\n<h3>Camera and files</h3><p>On compatible web browsers, QR scanning requests camera permission only when you start scanning; frames are decoded locally. In Android, choose an image or draft through the system document picker. CivicPost does not request access to your contacts, microphone or precise GPS. It can read files you choose and write exports to locations you select.</p>\n<h3>Deletion, retention and security</h3><p>Use Menu → Privacy, terms &amp; safety → Delete saved app data to remove CivicPost saved drafts, remembered location, saved lookup and notice acknowledgement, and clear the current letter. Individual saved drafts and lookups can also be removed separately. Browser site-data settings or Android app-storage settings can remove local app data. Clearing app data does not delete previously exported files, shared links, clipboard contents, emails or information retained by outside services. Contact those services for their retention/deletion rules. CivicPost does not operate a server-side draft store. HTTPS is used for app network requests, but no system can promise absolute security. Avoid entering unnecessary sensitive information.</p>\n<h3>Other providers</h3><ul><li><a href=\"https://opennorth.ca/privacy-policies/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open North privacy</a> and <a href=\"https://represent.opennorth.ca/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Represent service</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.bigdatacloud.com/privacy-and-cookie-policy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">BigDataCloud privacy</a></li><li><a href=\"https://policies.google.com/privacy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Google privacy</a> and <a href=\"https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Google advertising</a></li><li><a href=\"https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Microsoft privacy</a></li><li><a href=\"https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hosted-site provider privacy</a></li></ul>\n<h3>Policy changes</h3><p>This policy describes the current implementation. Material changes require an updated policy and, where required, new notices or consent. The notice date appears above.</p><h3>Developer and contact</h3><p>CivicPost Canada is provided by Abdullah Mohiuddin. For privacy requests, incorrect contact information, accessibility issues or other support: Public support email is not yet configured. This test build is not ready for public distribution.</p>"}, "terms": {"title": "Terms of use", "html": "<p>CivicPost Canada is an independent, nonpartisan drafting aid. It is not affiliated with, authorized by or acting for any government, political party, elected official or public office. It does not provide legal, medical or other professional advice.</p>\n<h3>Your choices and responsibilities</h3><p>Review facts, wording, recipients and attachments before sending. You control what you send and whether to send it. Use official procedures for emergencies, appeals, applications, legal notices and deadlines. A draft or email produced here is not proof of filing, delivery or receipt. No office response or particular outcome is promised.</p>\n<p>Use the app lawfully and respectfully. Do not use it for threats, harassment, impersonation, spam, unlawful discrimination, misleading statements or sharing another person's private information without a lawful basis. Only include information you are entitled to use. These rules apply to imported/shared drafts too. CivicPost does not review or endorse those drafts.</p>\n<h3>As-is availability and accuracy</h3><p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, the app, templates, directory and other information are provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of accuracy, completeness, fitness for a particular purpose, uninterrupted availability or error-free operation. Contacts, boundaries and responsibilities change. Check official sources and dates before relying on a result. Third-party websites, mail services and advertisements are outside the developer's control.</p>\n<h3>Limits and rights</h3><p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, the developer is not liable for losses arising from reliance on inaccurate information, failure or delay in delivery, third-party services, or your use or misuse of the app. Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or limits mandatory consumer or privacy rights. These terms do not promise that a disclaimer prevents a legal claim.</p>\n<h3>Content and services</h3><p>You retain rights in your own text. You do not grant CivicPost permission to publish your draft by using the editor. Public contact information and bundled software/data remain subject to their applicable licences. Google and other providers have their own terms. Features may change or become unavailable; keep your own copies of important correspondence. Advertisements are separate from civic information and do not influence recipient suggestions.</p><h3>Developer and contact</h3><p>CivicPost Canada is provided by Abdullah Mohiuddin. For privacy requests, incorrect contact information, accessibility issues or other support: Public support email is not yet configured. This test build is not ready for public distribution.</p>"}, "safety": {"title": "Safety and responsible use", "html": "<h3>Check before sending</h3><ul><li>Confirm the office, address, current officeholder and jurisdiction on an official source. Source dates and expiry warnings matter.</li><li>Postal results are possible matches. A postal code or approximate city does not prove your ward, riding, school board or Indigenous affiliation.</li><li>Check names, dates and facts. Keep the message truthful, respectful and specific. Imported campaign drafts may be inaccurate or biased; edit them in your own words.</li><li>Do not include passwords, bank details, identity documents, health records, children's details or a home address unless necessary and appropriate for the receiving office.</li><li>Review To and Cc: copied addresses are visible to recipients. Shared drafts, links and QR codes are readable by anyone who obtains them.</li></ul>\n<h3>Urgent matters and official processes</h3><p>CivicPost is not monitored for emergencies and does not contact emergency services. For immediate danger in Canada, call 911. For a legal deadline, formal complaint, application or appeal, use the required official channel and confirm receipt. Sending an ordinary email may not meet legal requirements.</p>\n<h3>External links and advertising</h3><p>Check a link's destination before providing personal information. Ad links are not government services and are not endorsements. Never pay an advertiser believing it is a required CivicPost step. All CivicPost drafting features work without viewing or interacting with ads.</p>\n<h3>Report a problem</h3><p>Use the support contact below to report inaccurate source information or an app/privacy issue. Include the office/source link and app version, but avoid sending your private letter or sensitive personal information unless needed. For a threat or urgent safety concern, use the appropriate emergency or official service.</p><h3>Developer and contact</h3><p>CivicPost Canada is provided by Abdullah Mohiuddin. For privacy requests, incorrect contact information, accessibility issues or other support: Public support email is not yet configured. This test build is not ready for public distribution.</p>"}, "sources": {"title": "Government information and sources", "html": "<p>CivicPost is independent and does not represent a government entity. Government information is drawn from published directories and source records; it may be outdated or incomplete.</p><p>In the app, choose an office's <strong>Details &amp; source</strong> to see its actual source URL, jurisdiction, retrieval date and any expiry warning. Menu → Coverage &amp; sources describes gaps. Secondary sources are labelled. A retrieval date does not certify an address or prove delivery.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.ourcommons.ca/Members/en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">House of Commons member directory</a></li><li><a href=\"https://sencanada.ca/en/senators/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Senate of Canada directory</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.canada.ca/en/government/dept.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Government of Canada departments and agencies</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.elections.ca/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Elections Canada</a></li><li><a href=\"https://represent.opennorth.ca/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open North Represent — independent data service</a></li></ul><p>Provincial, territorial, municipal and school contacts have individual source links in the directory. The bundled geographic database has its own provenance and licences in <a href=\"offline-postal/sources.html\">Offline database sources</a>. No address is generated from an official's name. Unsupported jurisdictions use official finder/service links instead.</p>"}}};
